  "semantics": [
    "Native5C04 receives a global IncTick pulse; there is no locally inferred recharge period. IncTick scans3000 runtime slots, active+enabled only, increments and caps to each supplied max. Current profile model retains its existing0..999 unit-domain bound.",
    "Native5C52 decodes unit signed word, AP signed word, menu unsigned word; C540 returns current pointer and advances2. Complete application payload lengths are2/8 respectively, transport framing is outside this decoder.",
    "SetTickMenu ignores inactive records; clamps absolute AP to0..max, replaces10C via bit permutation and updates action bits10/20 while preserving other100 bits. Menu restrictions do not replace ownership/innate capabilities or override automatic rest logic.",
    "Native activation/enabled flags are not HP. The adapter requires explicit activation metadata for pulse application and never invents unknown flags from current HP.",
    "Actual x86 counter/menu behavior is separately differential checked in native-battle-tick-check.json. Local session/revision/lifetime/receipt persistence are adapter contracts, not extra original wire fields."
  ]
